  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466364",
      "title": "Adding Query Params",
      "lectureOrder": 594,
      "videoOrder": 547,
      "sourceHash": "764f165bc46f297b0b8dc4e2d3a003d2bb6cd6a7358459cf27a4d342859fe6b2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "Instructor: Headers aren't the only thing you can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 6.39,
          "en": "For many API endpoints,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.39,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "you can also attach certain query parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 10.53,
          "en": "And of course, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.53,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "it depends on the API endpoint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "you are sending the request to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 16.71,
          "en": "which query parameters are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.71,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "For example, the Firebase REST API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 21.51,
          "en": "and you can learn that in the official docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.51,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "supports one query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 26.04,
          "en": "which effect we can immediately see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.04,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "You set parameters by adding the params key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "in that same config object where you added headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "and you set params equal to new HTTP params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 39.96,
          "en": "Now just as HTTP headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 43.71,
          "en": "you import HTTP params from at angular slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.71,
          "end": 45.513,
          "en": "common slash HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 51.15,
          "en": "Now HTTP params works a bit differently than HTTP headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "There you can call set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 58.14,
          "en": "and now you can set a para name and a value for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.14,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "And there, for example, you can set print.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "And that is a search param at query param",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 66.06,
          "en": "supported by Firebase. Print and you sent this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.06,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "to a value to pretty. And this just changes the format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "in which Firebase returns its data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 74.133,
          "en": "Now if we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 80.49,
          "en": "this loads, and now if I clear that and I click this again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 82.83,
          "en": "and we inspect this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.83,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "you see now it has this query parameter attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "to the end of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "And, of course, you could have added this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "to the URL yourself up there, too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "You could have added print equals pretty up there and add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "with an ampersand in between as many key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 102.84,
          "en": "as you need, or as your API endpoint supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.84,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "You can do that here in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "but by using this params config,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "it's a bit more convenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 111.87,
          "en": "because you don't need to concatenate a super long string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.87,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "You simply set them here with the set method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "Now, if you wanted to set multiple params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "you can simply do this by adding a search params constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "or whatever you wanna name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 126.51,
          "en": "Create your new params object there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 130.14,
          "en": "And now here you can call search params append",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "and append a new param key value pair like print pretty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "Important, however, search params, this object is immutable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 140.88,
          "en": "So you actually need to override this and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.88,
          "end": 143.28300000000002,
          "en": "this needs to be a variable with a new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.96,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "the result of append.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "So what you would do here in the end is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 150.39,
          "en": "you call append,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.39,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "and this returns a new HTTP params object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.48,
          "end": 156.3,
          "en": "And you store that new object which has these new key value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.3,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "pairs added to it in the search purpose variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "overriding the old one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "So you still have an HTTP params object in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "but a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 167.25,
          "en": "And you have... and if you have multiple key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.25,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "then you simply repeat that step with append.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "The old ones will be kept, but the new ones will be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.35,
          "en": "to a new HTTP params object which will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "replace the old one by storing it in it's same variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "So, here you could also have your custom key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "which is not supported by Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 186.12,
          "en": "but you can still set as it won't cause any harm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 189.09,
          "en": "And then you simply add your search params here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "for the params in your config object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "And this is how you can attach multiple params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 195.36,
          "en": "if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.36,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "We can see the effect here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 197.79,
          "en": "If I fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.79,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "now you see we have multiple search parameters attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 204.27,
          "en": "Again, you could have done that directly in the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.27,
          "end": 206.57999999999998,
          "en": "but by using the HTTP params object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 206.57999999999998,
          "end": 208.32,
          "en": "and the configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 208.32,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "it's a bit more convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 212.04,
          "en": "Now, by the way, in case you're wondering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 212.04,
          "end": 214.8,
          "en": "what these parameters do, custom key does nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 214.8,
          "end": 216.45,
          "en": "That's just something I came up with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 216.45,
          "end": 217.92000000000002,
          "en": "It's not supported by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 217.92000000000002,
          "end": 219.84,
          "en": "But, as I mentioned, it's also no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 219.84,
          "end": 221.07,
          "en": "if we add this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 221.07,
          "end": 223.5,
          "en": "Print pretty does something in the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 223.5,
          "end": 225.63,
          "en": "It prints this in a more pretty way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 228,
          "en": "It adds some extra white space and line breaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 228,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "so that this is more human readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "Absolutely does not matter for our app where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "we read this with our code anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "but I just wanted some example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 238.983,
          "en": "to show how to add query parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
